{"id":15179,"date":"2024-01-11T02:47:48","date_gmt":"2024-01-11T02:47:48","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/vdrs.com\/news-media\/van-dyk-in-2022-from-new-designs-to-startups-2\/"},"modified":"2024-01-11T04:16:56","modified_gmt":"2024-01-11T04:16:56","slug":"van-dyk-in-2023-major-projects-and-expansions","status":"publish","type":"page","link":"https:\/\/vdrs.com\/news-media\/van-dyk-in-2023-major-projects-and-expansions\/","title":{"rendered":"Van Dyk in 2023: Major Projects and Expansions"},"content":{"rendered":"<h2 style=\"text-align: center;\">A closer look at the major projects and expansions in Van Dyk&#8217;s 2023 portfolio<\/h2>\n<div style=\"height: 40px;\"><\/div>\n<figure id=\"attachment_15181\" aria-describedby=\"caption-attachment-15181\" style=\"width: 700px\" class=\"wp-caption aligncenter\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"wp-image-15181 size-full\" src=\"https:\/\/vdrs.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/01\/1-Intro-Slide.jpg\" alt=\"Van Dyk Recycling Solutions 2023 major projects\" width=\"700\" height=\"394\" srcset=\"https:\/\/vdrs.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/01\/1-Intro-Slide.jpg 700w, https:\/\/vdrs.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/01\/1-Intro-Slide-300x169.jpg 300w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 700px) 100vw, 700px\" \/><figcaption id=\"caption-attachment-15181\" class=\"wp-caption-text\">Major projects and expansions close 2023 for Van Dyk Recycling Solutions<\/figcaption><\/figure>\n<div style=\"height: 40px;\"><\/div>\n<h3 style=\"text-align: center; margin-bottom: 25px;\">Murphy Road Recycling<\/h3>\n<figure id=\"attachment_15182\" aria-describedby=\"caption-attachment-15182\" style=\"width: 700px\" class=\"wp-caption aligncenter\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"wp-image-15182 size-full\" src=\"https:\/\/vdrs.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/01\/2-Murphy-Road-Recycling.jpg\" alt=\"Murphy Road Recycling - Van Dyk Recycling Solutions 2023 major projects\" width=\"700\" height=\"394\" srcset=\"https:\/\/vdrs.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/01\/2-Murphy-Road-Recycling.jpg 700w, https:\/\/vdrs.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/01\/2-Murphy-Road-Recycling-300x169.jpg 300w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 700px) 100vw, 700px\" \/><figcaption id=\"caption-attachment-15182\" class=\"wp-caption-text\">Murphy Road Recycling, LLC was awarded the 2023 Recycling Facility of the Year title by the National Waste &amp; Recycling Association for their new single stream MRF in Berlin, CT (dubbed the All American MRF). Facilities with Van Dyk systems have won 7 out of the last 9 NWRA awards for Recycling Facility of the Year.<\/figcaption><\/figure>\n<div style=\"height: 40px;\"><\/div>\n<h3 style=\"text-align: center; margin-bottom: 25px;\">FCC Environmental Services<\/h3>\n<figure id=\"attachment_15183\" aria-describedby=\"caption-attachment-15183\" style=\"width: 700px\" class=\"wp-caption aligncenter\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"wp-image-15183 size-full\" src=\"https:\/\/vdrs.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/01\/3-FCC-CandD.jpg\" alt=\"FCC C&amp;D - Van Dyk Recycling Solutions 2023 major projects\" width=\"700\" height=\"394\" srcset=\"https:\/\/vdrs.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/01\/3-FCC-CandD.jpg 700w, https:\/\/vdrs.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/01\/3-FCC-CandD-300x169.jpg 300w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 700px) 100vw, 700px\" \/><figcaption id=\"caption-attachment-15183\" class=\"wp-caption-text\">In a deal with the Western Placer Waste Management Authority, FCC Environmental Services is building a 650,000-ton-per-year recycling complex to process the county\u2019s solid waste. The construction and demolition (C&amp;D) portion of the system is preparing for the commissioning stage. It will use density separation and optical sorting to process construction and demolition waste.<\/figcaption><\/figure>\n<div style=\"height: 40px;\"><\/div>\n<h3 style=\"text-align: center; margin-bottom: 25px;\">FCC Environmental Services MSW System<\/h3>\n<figure id=\"attachment_15184\" aria-describedby=\"caption-attachment-15184\" style=\"width: 700px\" class=\"wp-caption aligncenter\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"wp-image-15184 size-full\" src=\"https:\/\/vdrs.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/01\/4-FCC-MSW.jpg\" alt=\"FCC MSW - Van Dyk Recycling Solutions 2023 major projects\" width=\"700\" height=\"394\" srcset=\"https:\/\/vdrs.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/01\/4-FCC-MSW.jpg 700w, https:\/\/vdrs.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/01\/4-FCC-MSW-300x169.jpg 300w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 700px) 100vw, 700px\" \/><figcaption id=\"caption-attachment-15184\" class=\"wp-caption-text\">Following completion of the C&amp;D system at FCC Environmental Services\u2019 Placer County MRF, installation will begin on the municipal solid waste (MSW) system. Equipment has already been delivered. The system will separate household waste to divert recyclables and organics from landfill in compliance with California\u2019s SB-1383 regulation.<\/figcaption><\/figure>\n<div style=\"height: 40px;\"><\/div>\n<h3 style=\"text-align: center; margin-bottom: 25px;\">WM Automated Single-Stream Systems<\/h3>\n<figure id=\"attachment_15185\" aria-describedby=\"caption-attachment-15185\" style=\"width: 700px\" class=\"wp-caption aligncenter\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"wp-image-15185 size-full\" src=\"https:\/\/vdrs.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/01\/5-WM-logo.jpg\" alt=\"WM residential single stream systems - Van Dyk Recycling Solutions 2023 major projects\" width=\"700\" height=\"394\" srcset=\"https:\/\/vdrs.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/01\/5-WM-logo.jpg 700w, https:\/\/vdrs.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/01\/5-WM-logo-300x169.jpg 300w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 700px) 100vw, 700px\" \/><figcaption id=\"caption-attachment-15185\" class=\"wp-caption-text\">In 2024, Van Dyk looks forward to kicking off installation on two brand new, highly automated residential single-stream sorting systems in Texas, one in the New Braunfels area between Austin and San Antonio and one in the Fort Worth area. Both will be owned and operated by WM.<\/figcaption><\/figure>\n<div style=\"height: 40px;\"><\/div>\n<h3 style=\"text-align: center; margin-bottom: 25px;\">WM Invests in Upgrading Facilities Throughout North America<\/h3>\n<figure id=\"attachment_15186\" aria-describedby=\"caption-attachment-15186\" style=\"width: 700px\" class=\"wp-caption aligncenter\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"wp-image-15186 size-full\" src=\"https:\/\/vdrs.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/01\/6-WM-Cleveland.jpg\" alt=\"WM new and upgraded facilities - Van Dyk Recycling Solutions 2023 major projects\" width=\"700\" height=\"394\" srcset=\"https:\/\/vdrs.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/01\/6-WM-Cleveland.jpg 700w, https:\/\/vdrs.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/01\/6-WM-Cleveland-300x169.jpg 300w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 700px) 100vw, 700px\" \/><figcaption id=\"caption-attachment-15186\" class=\"wp-caption-text\">WM has announced plans to make substantial investments in new and upgraded recycling facilities throughout North America. Van Dyk is proud to collaborate with WM on many of these projects, including: Woodinville, Washington; Cleveland, Ohio; Germantown, Wisconsin; Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania; and Surprise, Arizona.<\/figcaption><\/figure>\n<div style=\"height: 40px;\"><\/div>\n<h3 style=\"text-align: center; margin-bottom: 25px;\">Crown Shred &amp; Recycling<\/h3>\n<figure id=\"attachment_15187\" aria-describedby=\"caption-attachment-15187\" style=\"width: 700px\" class=\"wp-caption aligncenter\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"size-full wp-image-15187\" src=\"https:\/\/vdrs.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/01\/7-Crown-Shred-and-Recycling.jpg\" alt=\"Crown Shred and Recycling - Van Dyk Recycling Solutions 2023 major projects\" width=\"700\" height=\"394\" srcset=\"https:\/\/vdrs.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/01\/7-Crown-Shred-and-Recycling.jpg 700w, https:\/\/vdrs.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/01\/7-Crown-Shred-and-Recycling-300x169.jpg 300w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 700px) 100vw, 700px\" \/><figcaption id=\"caption-attachment-15187\" class=\"wp-caption-text\">Crown Shred &amp; Recycling Inc. of Regina, Saskatchewan, is building a brand new 30-ton-per-hour single stream system to increase the volume of material processed by the company. The highly automated technology is anticipated to also increase recycling rates in the area.<\/figcaption><\/figure>\n<div style=\"height: 40px;\"><\/div>\n<h3 style=\"text-align: center; margin-bottom: 25px;\">GFL&#8217;s &#8220;Future-Ready&#8221; MRF<\/h3>\n<figure id=\"attachment_15188\" aria-describedby=\"caption-attachment-15188\" style=\"width: 700px\" class=\"wp-caption aligncenter\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"wp-image-15188 size-full\" src=\"https:\/\/vdrs.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/01\/8-GFL-logo.jpg\" alt=\"GFL's MRF - Van Dyk Recycling Solutions 2023 major projects\" width=\"700\" height=\"394\" srcset=\"https:\/\/vdrs.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/01\/8-GFL-logo.jpg 700w, https:\/\/vdrs.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/01\/8-GFL-logo-300x169.jpg 300w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 700px) 100vw, 700px\" \/><figcaption id=\"caption-attachment-15188\" class=\"wp-caption-text\">GFL\u2019s Edmonton location is rebuilding their MRF in a brand new building with the latest technology from Van Dyk Recycling Solutions. The highly modernized system will feature a flexible and \u201cfuture ready\u201d design to meet emerging material sorting requirements.<\/figcaption><\/figure>\n<div style=\"height: 40px;\"><\/div>\n<h3 style=\"text-align: center; margin-bottom: 25px;\">Penn Waste System Rebuild<\/h3>\n<figure id=\"attachment_15189\" aria-describedby=\"caption-attachment-15189\" style=\"width: 700px\" class=\"wp-caption aligncenter\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"wp-image-15189 size-full\" src=\"https:\/\/vdrs.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/01\/9-Penn-Waste.jpg\" alt=\"Penn Waste system - Van Dyk Recycling Solutions 2023 major projects\" width=\"700\" height=\"394\" srcset=\"https:\/\/vdrs.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/01\/9-Penn-Waste.jpg 700w, https:\/\/vdrs.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/01\/9-Penn-Waste-300x169.jpg 300w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 700px) 100vw, 700px\" \/><figcaption id=\"caption-attachment-15189\" class=\"wp-caption-text\">After Penn Waste suffered a devastating fire, they put forth a well-coordinated effort to rebuild their system in just one year. To replace its container line, the company turned to Van Dyk Recycling Solutions and Pellenc ST to supply six Mistral+ CONNECT optical sorters, which brought an increase in the plant\u2019s recovery capabilities.<\/figcaption><\/figure>\n<div style=\"height: 40px;\"><\/div>\n<h3 style=\"text-align: center; margin-bottom: 25px;\">NOVA Circular Solutions<\/h3>\n<figure id=\"attachment_15190\" aria-describedby=\"caption-attachment-15190\" style=\"width: 700px\" class=\"wp-caption aligncenter\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"wp-image-15190 size-full\" src=\"https:\/\/vdrs.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/01\/10-Nova-Chemical.jpg\" alt=\"Nova Chemical - Van Dyk Recycling Solutions 2023 major projects\" width=\"700\" height=\"394\" srcset=\"https:\/\/vdrs.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/01\/10-Nova-Chemical.jpg 700w, https:\/\/vdrs.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/01\/10-Nova-Chemical-300x169.jpg 300w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 700px) 100vw, 700px\" \/><figcaption id=\"caption-attachment-15190\" class=\"wp-caption-text\">Van Dyk is a contributor to NOVA Circular Solutions\u2019 first mechanical recycling facility, which will convert postconsumer plastic films into recycled polyethylene with a capacity of over 100 million pounds per year. Van Dyk is providing optical sorters and conveying equipment for this state-of-the-art recycling facility.<\/figcaption><\/figure>\n<div style=\"height: 40px;\"><\/div>\n<h3 style=\"text-align: center; margin-bottom: 25px;\">Freepoint Eco-Systems<\/h3>\n<figure id=\"attachment_15191\" aria-describedby=\"caption-attachment-15191\" style=\"width: 700px\" class=\"wp-caption aligncenter\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"wp-image-15191 size-full\" src=\"https:\/\/vdrs.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/01\/11-Freepoint-Eco-Systems.jpg\" alt=\"Freepoint Eco-Systems - Van Dyk Recycling Solutions 2023 major projects\" width=\"700\" height=\"394\" srcset=\"https:\/\/vdrs.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/01\/11-Freepoint-Eco-Systems.jpg 700w, https:\/\/vdrs.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/01\/11-Freepoint-Eco-Systems-300x169.jpg 300w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 700px) 100vw, 700px\" \/><figcaption id=\"caption-attachment-15191\" class=\"wp-caption-text\">Freepoint Eco-Systems is partnering with Van Dyk to develop a large mixed plastics preprocessing plant that will use elliptical separation and optical sorting to recover plastics from MRF residue. Startup is expected in 2024.<\/figcaption><\/figure>\n<div style=\"height: 40px;\"><\/div>\n<h3 style=\"text-align: center; margin-bottom: 25px;\">Evergreen<\/h3>\n<figure id=\"attachment_15192\" aria-describedby=\"caption-attachment-15192\" style=\"width: 700px\" class=\"wp-caption aligncenter\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"wp-image-15192 size-full\" src=\"https:\/\/vdrs.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/01\/12-Evergreen.jpg\" alt=\"Evergreen - Van Dyk Recycling Solutions 2023 major projects\" width=\"700\" height=\"394\" srcset=\"https:\/\/vdrs.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/01\/12-Evergreen.jpg 700w, https:\/\/vdrs.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/01\/12-Evergreen-300x169.jpg 300w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 700px) 100vw, 700px\" \/><figcaption id=\"caption-attachment-15192\" class=\"wp-caption-text\">Evergreen is adding four new TOMRA Flakesorters to process recycled polyethylene terephthalate (PET) into food-grade recycled rPET pellets used to manufacture new bottles.<\/figcaption><\/figure>\n<div style=\"height: 40px;\"><\/div>\n<h3 style=\"text-align: center; margin-bottom: 25px;\">Smimo Food Waste Depackaging<\/h3>\n<figure id=\"attachment_15193\" aria-describedby=\"caption-attachment-15193\" style=\"width: 700px\" class=\"wp-caption aligncenter\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"wp-image-15193 size-full\" src=\"https:\/\/vdrs.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/01\/13-Smimo-depacker.jpg\" alt=\"Smimo depacker - Van Dyk Recycling Solutions 2023 major projects\" width=\"700\" height=\"394\" srcset=\"https:\/\/vdrs.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/01\/13-Smimo-depacker.jpg 700w, https:\/\/vdrs.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/01\/13-Smimo-depacker-300x169.jpg 300w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 700px) 100vw, 700px\" \/><figcaption id=\"caption-attachment-15193\" class=\"wp-caption-text\">A Smimo food waste depacking machine by manufacturer Smicon is being installed in Sunnyvale, California, as part of an organics recycling system. These depacking machines turn food waste into feedstock for renewable energy while diverting the material from landfill. This is the sixth Smimo machine to be installed in the U.S.<\/figcaption><\/figure>\n<div style=\"height: 40px;\"><\/div>\n<h3 style=\"text-align: center; margin-bottom: 25px;\">Van Dyk Supplies 37 Balers in 2023<\/h3>\n<figure id=\"attachment_15194\" aria-describedby=\"caption-attachment-15194\" style=\"width: 700px\" class=\"wp-caption aligncenter\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"wp-image-15194 size-full\" src=\"https:\/\/vdrs.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/01\/14-Balers.jpg\" alt=\"Balers installed in 2023 - Van Dyk Recycling Solutions 2023 major projects\" width=\"700\" height=\"394\" srcset=\"https:\/\/vdrs.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/01\/14-Balers.jpg 700w, https:\/\/vdrs.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/01\/14-Balers-300x169.jpg 300w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 700px) 100vw, 700px\" \/><figcaption id=\"caption-attachment-15194\" class=\"wp-caption-text\">2023 was a good year for supplying balers. Van Dyk put 25 balers into MRF projects and 12 balers into high-volume commercial and high-grade facilities. Sites include Pioneer Industries, Fontana Recycling, Taylor Recycling and WM Paper Valley.<\/figcaption><\/figure>\n<div style=\"height: 40px;\"><\/div>\n<h3 style=\"text-align: center; margin-bottom: 25px;\">Bollegraaf&#8217;s Newest System<\/h3>\n<figure id=\"attachment_15195\" aria-describedby=\"caption-attachment-15195\" style=\"width: 700px\" class=\"wp-caption aligncenter\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"wp-image-15195 size-full\" src=\"https:\/\/vdrs.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/01\/15-Peute-Recycling.jpg\" alt=\"Peute Recycling - Van Dyk Recycling Solutions 2023 major projects\" width=\"700\" height=\"394\" srcset=\"https:\/\/vdrs.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/01\/15-Peute-Recycling.jpg 700w, https:\/\/vdrs.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/01\/15-Peute-Recycling-300x169.jpg 300w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 700px) 100vw, 700px\" \/><figcaption id=\"caption-attachment-15195\" class=\"wp-caption-text\">Our manufacturing partner, Bollegraaf Recycling Solutions, unveils its newest system outside Rotterdam, Netherlands, in a grand opening. The Peute Recycling plant processes 80 tons per hour of paper, cardboard and plastic film using the latest generation equipment, including the 880 antiwrapping screen, the 440 antiwrapping screen and three adjacent balers, two of which are the next-gen Bollegraaf balers, HBC150S.<\/figcaption><\/figure>\n<div style=\"height: 40px;\"><\/div>\n<h3 style=\"text-align: center; margin-bottom: 25px;\">Bollegraaf System at R\u00e9union Island<\/h3>\n<figure id=\"attachment_15196\" aria-describedby=\"caption-attachment-15196\" style=\"width: 700px\" class=\"wp-caption aligncenter\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"wp-image-15196 size-full\" src=\"https:\/\/vdrs.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/01\/16-La-Reunion.jpg\" alt=\"La Reunion - Van Dyk Recycling Solutions 2023 major projects\" width=\"700\" height=\"394\" srcset=\"https:\/\/vdrs.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/01\/16-La-Reunion.jpg 700w, https:\/\/vdrs.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/01\/16-La-Reunion-300x169.jpg 300w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 700px) 100vw, 700px\" \/><figcaption id=\"caption-attachment-15196\" class=\"wp-caption-text\">This upcoming Bollegraaf system will process 50 tons per hour of MSW material on the French island of R\u00e9union, off the coast of Madagascar. Instead of going to landfill, the materials will be sorted into seven different fractions and the residue will be turned into fuel to provide power to 11,000 households on the island.<\/figcaption><\/figure>\n<div style=\"height: 40px;\"><\/div>\n<h3 style=\"text-align: center; margin-bottom: 25px;\">Zoomlion<\/h3>\n<figure id=\"attachment_15197\" aria-describedby=\"caption-attachment-15197\" style=\"width: 700px\" class=\"wp-caption aligncenter\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"wp-image-15197 size-full\" src=\"https:\/\/vdrs.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/01\/17-Zoomlion.jpg\" alt=\"Zoomlion Ghana - Van Dyk Recycling Solutions 2023 major projects\" width=\"700\" height=\"394\" srcset=\"https:\/\/vdrs.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/01\/17-Zoomlion.jpg 700w, https:\/\/vdrs.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/01\/17-Zoomlion-300x169.jpg 300w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 700px) 100vw, 700px\" \/><figcaption id=\"caption-attachment-15197\" class=\"wp-caption-text\">Our manufacturing partner, Lubo Recycling Solutions, is wrapping up the first of seven MSW lines for Zoomlion in Ghana. The project features seven MSW lines in total: two fixed, four semi-mobile and one retrofit, in which all machinery will be replaced. The main goal of these lines is to provide local farmers with high-quality topsoil to increase local food production and security.<\/figcaption><\/figure>\n<div style=\"height: 40px;\"><\/div>\n<h3 style=\"text-align: center; margin-bottom: 25px;\">Van Dyk University<\/h3>\n<figure id=\"attachment_15198\" aria-describedby=\"caption-attachment-15198\" style=\"width: 700px\" class=\"wp-caption aligncenter\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"wp-image-15198 size-full\" src=\"https:\/\/vdrs.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/01\/19-Van-Dyk-University.jpg\" alt=\"Van Dyk University - Van Dyk Recycling Solutions 2023 major projects\" width=\"700\" height=\"394\" srcset=\"https:\/\/vdrs.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/01\/19-Van-Dyk-University.jpg 700w, https:\/\/vdrs.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/01\/19-Van-Dyk-University-300x169.jpg 300w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 700px) 100vw, 700px\" \/><figcaption id=\"caption-attachment-15198\" class=\"wp-caption-text\">Van Dyk offers training courses for Bollegraaf Balers, Tomra Autosort and Pellenc ST Mistral+. Want to train your operators on one of these machines? Call us at <a href=\"tel:2039671100\">203-967-1100<\/a> to book your spot in 2024.<\/figcaption><\/figure>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>A closer look at the major projects and expansions in Van Dyk&#8217;s 2023 portfolio Murphy Road Recycling FCC Environmental Services FCC Environmental Services MSW System WM Automated Single-Stream Systems WM Invests in Upgrading Facilities Throughout North America Crown Shred &amp; Recycling GFL&#8217;s &#8220;Future-Ready&#8221; MRF Penn Waste System Rebuild NOVA Circular Solutions Freepoint Eco-Systems Evergreen Smimo &hellip; <\/p>\n<p class=\"link-more\"><a href=\"https:\/\/vdrs.com\/news-media\/van-dyk-in-2023-major-projects-and-expansions\/\" class=\"more-link\">Continue reading<span class=\"screen-reader-text\"> &#8220;Van Dyk in 2023: Major Projects and Expansions&#8221;<\/span><\/a><\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":4,"featured_media":15204,"parent":105,"menu_order":84,"comment_status":"closed","ping_status":"closed","template":"template-fullwidth.php","meta":{"_acf_changed":false,"footnotes":""},"class_list":["post-15179","page","type-page","status-publish","has-post-thu